# Domain-scoped OBO user access + Team-gated graph data access

Context:
Enforce per-domain, on-behalf-of (OBO) access for graph data. In Databricks
Apps, every non-build Unity Catalog data read now runs as the signed-in user
(their forwarded token), so UC governance applies per user instead of the app
service principal. Backends that carry no UC identity (Lakebase Postgres,
Neo4j) are gated by Team membership — the caller must hold at least the Viewer
role on the loaded domain. Build (view/triplestore materialisation) stays on
the control-plane service principal. The MCP server forwards the end-user
identity so the same rules apply to MCP-driven reads. All data-plane reads are
fail-closed: no forwarded user token → access denied (never a silent SP
fallback). Local dev is unaffected (OBO and the Team gate are no-ops outside
App mode). Design + plan: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-26-domain-obo-graph-access-design.md`,
`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-26-domain-obo-graph-access.md`.

Changes:

1. `src/back/core/databricks/request_identity.py`
   New request-scoped `RequestIdentity` (email, user_token, app_role,
   domain_role) backed by a `ContextVar`, with set/get/reset helpers.
2. `src/shared/fastapi/main.py`
   `PermissionMiddleware` stamps the request identity (and `request.state.user_token`
   from `x-forwarded-access-token`) around every `call_next`, with try/finally reset.
3. `src/back/core/helpers/DatabricksHelpers.py`, `src/back/core/helpers/__init__.py`
   Added `get_data_plane_client(domain, settings)` — mints a user-token client in
   App mode (fail-closed: raises `AuthorizationError` when no user token), delegates
   to the SP client in local mode. Exported from the helpers package.
4. `src/back/core/databricks/SQLWarehouse.py`
   Connection pools keyed by caller identity (`sp` vs `user:<sha256(token)[:16]>`)
   so a connection minted for one user is never reused for another.
5. `src/api/routers/internal/_graph_access.py`
   New `assert_domain_graph_read(request)` Team gate: no-op in local mode, App
   admins bypass, everyone else needs Viewer+ on the loaded domain.
6. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py`, `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
   SPARQL / GraphQL / triples / neighbors / clusters / DQ / inferred / node-context
   reads run via `get_data_plane_client` and are guarded by `assert_domain_graph_read`.
7. `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaBase.py`, `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py`
   Delta read path overrides the token with the request user token (OBO) in App
   mode; Lakebase/Neo4j keep SP + Team-gate (documented via intent comments).
8. `src/api/routers/internal/mapping.py`, `.../VirtualAttributeService.py`,
   `.../NodeContextService.py`
   Mapping preview / test-query / UC browse, Class Action `EXECUTE`, and
   virtual-attribute compute repointed to `get_data_plane_client`. LLM/wizard
   (model-serving) paths left on the control-plane.
9. `src/mcp-server/server/http_client.py`, `.../session.py`, `.../session_scope.py`
   MCP forwards the end-user identity: `set_forwarded_identity` / `_merged_headers`
   attach `x-forwarded-email` / `x-forwarded-access-token` (+ M2M `Authorization`)
   on every `_get` / `_post`; the session-scope middleware binds the inbound
   headers per tool call and clears them in `finally`; session sets the server mode.
10. Docs — `docs/deployment.md` (§E new "On-Behalf-Of (OBO) data-plane identity"),
    `docs/features.md` (Security OBO + per-domain gating bullets, per-identity SQL
    pooling), `docs/data-access.md` (MCP identity forwarding note).

